{"lean_source":"namespace VeriSlop\nstructure Input where\n  n : Int\n  edges : List (List Int)\n\ndef conforms (input : Input) : Prop :=\n  0 ≤ input.n ∧ input.n ≤ 10 ∧\n  ∀ edge ∈ input.edges, ∃ u v : Int,\n    edge = [u, v] ∧ 0 ≤ u ∧ u < input.n ∧ 0 ≤ v ∧ v < input.n\n\ntheorem conforms_empty : conforms ⟨0, []⟩ := by\n  simp [conforms]\nend VeriSlop\n","formalization":{"status":"unsupported_domain","error":"The required executable contract cannot faithfully represent the specified output and implementation restrictions in the supplied registered frontend. The Lean source declares the actual input fields and establishes a concrete satisfiability witness; it does not assert that the remaining obligations are discharged.","gaps":[{"obligations":["O1","O3","O5","E1"],"description":"The required return value is JSON null for any directed cycle, otherwise a list of two-element integer lists. The supplied AST sorts provide no nullable-list sort or documented serialization mapping that makes Unit or Except produce this exact null-or-list output. Substituting an error constructor, output record, or empty list for null changes the specification."},{"obligations":["S1"],"description":"The registered mathematical term and formula language cannot establish restrictions on Python dependencies, external I/O, file reads, network use, printing, or retained state."}],"preserved_obligations":["D1","A1","O1","O2","O3","O4","O5","S1","E1"],"preserved_requirements":{"input":"solve receives one JSON object with integer n from 0 through 10 and edges containing directed pairs [u,v].","assumption":"Caller inputs conform to the graph specification. The empty graph provides a satisfiability witness.","output":"Ignore duplicate directed edges. Return JSON null whenever any directed cycle exists anywhere, including self-loops and disconnected components. For acyclic inputs return precisely the unique original edges having no alternate path of at least two edges, as two-element lists sorted lexicographically by source then destination. Preserve every directed reachability relation, include no redundant edges, and represent isolated vertices implicitly. Edgeless graphs including n=0 return an empty list.","examples":"The n=3 graph with edges [[0,1],[1,2],[0,2],[0,2]] returns [[0,1],[1,2]]. The n=1 graph with edges [[0,0]] returns null.","implementation":"solution.py exposes pure deterministic Python 3 solve(data), returns JSON-serializable values, uses only the standard library, performs no external I/O, and retains no state across calls."},"required_extension":"A registered executable nullable-list sort with explicit null-or-list JSON serialization and branch semantics, together with implementation checks for the S1 restrictions. Opaque Lean acceptance cannot substitute for the requested strict Python TESTED assurance."}}